>## Show a not-a-forall-type error as a string
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>term notAForallTypeError = λe.let typ := checking.NotAForallTypeError[`type`] e in let args := checking.NotAForallTypeError[typeArguments] e in strings.concat ["not a forall type: ", print.model.type typ, ". Trying to apply ", literals.printInt32 (lists.length args), " type argument(s): ", formatting.showList print.model.type args]
